    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin \\theta$ and $\\cos \\theta$. Enter both signed coefficients, including zero when needed.\n\n$\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\pi\\right)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin \\theta+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos \\theta$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\n\nThe fixed angle has exact values\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right)=-1,\\qquad \\sin\\left(\\pi\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $u=\\theta$ and $v=\\pi$, then simplify the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\pi\\right)&=\\sin \\theta\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right)+\\cos \\theta\\sin\\left(\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin \\theta\\left(-1\\right)+\\cos \\theta\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\sin \\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested coefficients are $-1$ and $0$, respectively. A negative coefficient goes inside its blank.",
